(304944, 21803, 8682, '<td valign="top">Beatiful picture... I love the colours</td>', 'Beatiful picture... I love the colours', '2003-05-22 11:07:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(305022, 21952, 7010, '<td valign="top">The brightness and the saturation of the colours work very appealing.  You also did well on the composition. It''s a tiny bit out of focus and there is an over-exposed area on the left of the blue candy. also, the image has kind of a magenta cast. (e.g. the shadow areas of the sugar) <br/>Technique: 2/4<br/>Composition : 2/3<br/>Originality/meeting the challenge: 2/3<br/>Total = 6</td>', 'The brightness and the saturation of the colours work very appealing.  You also did well on the composition. It''s a tiny bit out of focus and there is an over-exposed area on the left of the blue candy. also, the image has kind of a magenta cast. (e.g. the shadow areas of the sugar) Technique: 2/4Composition : 2/3Originality/meeting the challenge: 2/3Total = 6', '2003-05-22 14:36:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(305049, 21843, 8530, '<td valign="top">Inasmuch as there are contrasting colors here, the blend near the center sort of reduces the impact of the ''contrast''. Interesting idea, though.</td>', 'Inasmuch as there are contrasting colors here, the blend near the center sort of reduces the impact of the ''contrast''. Interesting idea, though.', '2003-05-22 15:06:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(305050, 21578, 8530, '<td valign="top">This does contrast, but it''s a little too abstract for my tastes. Are these pieces of fruit? They kind of look it.</td>', 'This does contrast, but it''s a little too abstract for my tastes. Are these pieces of fruit? They kind of look it.', '2003-05-22 15:07:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(305051, 21847, 8530, '<td valign="top">Very good match to topic, and nice close-up.</td>', 'Very good match to topic, and nice close-up.', '2003-05-22 15:08:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(305052, 21740, 8530, '<td valign="top">Hmm. The red/green contrast is there, but the yellow undermines this completely. Still, nice framing of the rose. It''s also interesting how the top almost looks like a road fading into infinity.</td>', 'Hmm. The red/green contrast is there, but the yellow undermines this completely. Still, nice framing of the rose. It''s also interesting how the top almost looks like a road fading into infinity.', '2003-05-22 15:09:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(305053, 21857, 8530, '<td valign="top">With the yellow between the green/red, and the space between the dark/light, I''m afraid this picture doesn''t really say ''contrasting colours'' to me. This might have been better in one of the other colour-related contests.</td>', 'With the yellow between the green/red, and the space between the dark/light, I''m afraid this picture doesn''t really say ''contrasting colours'' to me. This might have been better in one of the other colour-related contests.', '2003-05-22 15:10:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(305056, 21780, 8530, '<td valign="top">Very nice. The non-contrasting colours in the photo are very neutral, which lets the picture be on the eggplant/dish combo. This would make a great magazine advertisement for... well, something. That''s a compliment, I promise.</td>', 'Very nice. The non-contrasting colours in the photo are very neutral, which lets the picture be on the eggplant/dish combo. This would make a great magazine advertisement for... well, something. That''s a compliment, I promise.', '2003-05-22 15:11:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(305059, 21971, 8530, '<td valign="top">This would have worked better for me if staged with, say, multiple Sharpies of each colour, or perhaps against a backdrop of coloured-in squares on a whiteboard, or something along those lines. As it is, it sort of feels like you picked the first couple contrasting coloured objects you had handy, stuck them next to each other, and gave up.</td>', 'This would have worked better for me if staged with, say, multiple Sharpies of each colour, or perhaps against a backdrop of coloured-in squares on a whiteboard, or something along those lines. As it is, it sort of feels like you picked the first couple contrasting coloured objects you had handy, stuck them next to each other, and gave up.', '2003-05-22 15:14:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(305060, 21641, 8530, '<td valign="top">Very pretty, and definitely fitting the ''complementary'' part. An angle that overlapped leaf and flower would have been even nicer.</td>', 'Very pretty, and definitely fitting the ''complementary'' part. An angle that overlapped leaf and flower would have been even nicer.', '2003-05-22 15:15:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(305061, 21930, 8530, '<td valign="top">Heh, interesting concept, and very nice picture, but it might have served the colouring expectations better to take it against a different background -- there''s a bit too much green-flowing-to-green to really emphasize the topic, though the focal object certainly does.</td>', 'Heh, interesting concept, and very nice picture, but it might have served the colouring expectations better to take it against a different background -- there''s a bit too much green-flowing-to-green to really emphasize the topic, though the focal object certainly does.', '2003-05-22 15:16:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(305063, 21927, 8530, '<td valign="top">Okay, this is just plain cool. I know, that''s not a terribly useful comment, but it is my reaction. I like the way that the outer top to inner center edges flow light to dark in equivalent contrast levels, very nice emphasis (whether intentional or not).</td>', 'Okay, this is just plain cool. I know, that''s not a terribly useful comment, but it is my reaction. I like the way that the outer top to inner center edges flow light to dark in equivalent contrast levels, very nice emphasis (whether intentional or not).', '2003-05-22 15:17:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(305065, 21932, 8530, '<td valign="top">Very, very nice choice of angle and placement. Even with the slightly higher orange concentration, the contrast between the complementary colours is obviously the focus of the picture. And it''s pretty, to boot!</td>', 'Very, very nice choice of angle and placement. Even with the slightly higher orange concentration, the contrast between the complementary colours is obviously the focus of the picture. And it''s pretty, to boot!', '2003-05-22 15:18:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(305066, 21741, 8530, '<td valign="top">Huh.<br/> <br/>It fits the theme, and it''s an interesting photo, but I think the background probably should have been another shade, and the angle might have been better on the sides of the lighter -- the shininess of the metal draws the eye away from the contrast and onto the shiny yellow bits.</td>', 'Huh. It fits the theme, and it''s an interesting photo, but I think the background probably should have been another shade, and the angle might have been better on the sides of the lighter -- the shininess of the metal draws the eye away from the contrast and onto the shiny yellow bits.', '2003-05-22 15:20:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(305067, 21911, 8530, '<td valign="top">While I see what you were doing here, and the way the reflection comes off the sky is very nice, I''m afraid the building colour fades into neutrality enough that it doesn''t highlight the ''complementary'' bit for me.</td>', 'While I see what you were doing here, and the way the reflection comes off the sky is very nice, I''m afraid the building colour fades into neutrality enough that it doesn''t highlight the ''complementary'' bit for me.', '2003-05-22 15:20:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(305073, 21669, 7010, '<td valign="top">Very nice! I love the contrast of the two elements. Composition is well balanced, you gave both elements enough weight. The red border spoils this wonderful image a bit imho. Very intelligent shot!<br/>Technique: 3/4<br/>Composition : 3/3<br/>Originality/meeting the challenge: 2/3<br/>Total = 8<br/></td>', 'Very nice! I love the contrast of the two elements. Composition is well balanced, you gave both elements enough weight. The red border spoils this wonderful image a bit imho. Very intelligent shot!Technique: 3/4Composition : 3/3Originality/meeting the challenge: 2/3Total = 8', '2003-05-22 15:30:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(305090, 21857, 7778, '<td valign="top">Considering the nature of the bulk of available submissions under this topic, how refreshing to find one with a ''range'' extending beyond ''topicality''. In other words, it can ''hold it''s own'', and will remain a great shot even after this challenge is over. <br/> <br/>I''m so happy with this photo, I don''t even mind the velcro!  :-)</td>', 'Considering the nature of the bulk of available submissions under this topic, how refreshing to find one with a ''range'' extending beyond ''topicality''. In other words, it can ''hold it''s own'', and will remain a great shot even after this challenge is over.  I''m so happy with this photo, I don''t even mind the velcro!  :-)', '2003-05-22 15:54:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(305091, 21866, 7778, '<td valign="top">Frankly, perhaps not a ''great'', coz it''s a ''limited'' albeit ''topical'' pleasure. On the other hand, I can see how hard it is to resist taking it. :-) The colours are just ''wild'' together. Eat your heart out IKEA!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Frankly, perhaps not a ''great'', coz it''s a ''limited'' albeit ''topical'' pleasure. On the other hand, I can see how hard it is to resist taking it. :-) The colours are just ''wild'' together. Eat your heart out IKEA! ', '2003-05-22 16:02:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(305093, 21830, 8530, '<td valign="top">Wow, very nice way to handle the focus of the challenge, and nice close-up shot. Is this a Coleus leaf? I like the orientation of the color change as well.</td>', 'Wow, very nice way to handle the focus of the challenge, and nice close-up shot. Is this a Coleus leaf? I like the orientation of the color change as well.', '2003-05-22 16:14:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(305094, 21850, 8530, '<td valign="top">I think the focus should have been closer-in to the bike, perhaps cropped there or zoomed in as appropriate. But it''s good it''s an obvious splash of colour against a fairly neutral background, which helps draw the eye.</td>', 'I think the focus should have been closer-in to the bike, perhaps cropped there or zoomed in as appropriate. But it''s good it''s an obvious splash of colour against a fairly neutral background, which helps draw the eye.', '2003-05-22 16:15:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(305096, 21968, 8530, '<td valign="top">It took me a moment to discover any sort of complementary colour here, and there''s far too much expanse of neutral colour between them to make it obvious. The off-center nature of the subject just makes it harder. The natural focus point of the center does not contain the complementary colours (assuming the focus is red/green, and not some sort of very subtle tan/blue vein thing), so you have to search for it. For a topic like this, I prefer a lack of subtlety. In other topics this photograph would probably have rated more highly with me.</td>', 'It took me a moment to discover any sort of complementary colour here, and there''s far too much expanse of neutral colour between them to make it obvious. The off-center nature of the subject just makes it harder. The natural focus point of the center does not contain the complementary colours (assuming the focus is red/green, and not some sort of very subtle tan/blue vein thing), so you have to search for it. For a topic like this, I prefer a lack of subtlety. In other topics this photograph would probably have rated more highly with me.', '2003-05-22 16:17:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(305097, 21914, 8530, '<td valign="top">Hmm, I begin to suspect this will be a common theme. This is nice, however; it meets the criterion and the overlap of leaf and peta, particularly at the top left where the deeper colours meet, captures the essence of the topic nicely. It is also framed well, with the focal points surrounding the center.</td>', 'Hmm, I begin to suspect this will be a common theme. This is nice, however; it meets the criterion and the overlap of leaf and peta, particularly at the top left where the deeper colours meet, captures the essence of the topic nicely. It is also framed well, with the focal points surrounding the center.', '2003-05-22 16:18:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(305099, 21978, 8530, '<td valign="top">This is interesting, and the impulse to place it against a black background a good one, but why so off-center? I realize dead-center focal points are considered boring by a lot of people, but when the only part of the image with colour is your focal point, centering seems more natural. This feels awkward to me.<br/> <br/>The actual topical element is lovely, though. I''d hate to have wash all that off!</td>', 'This is interesting, and the impulse to place it against a black background a good one, but why so off-center? I realize dead-center focal points are considered boring by a lot of people, but when the only part of the image with colour is your focal point, centering seems more natural. This feels awkward to me. The actual topical element is lovely, though. I''d hate to have wash all that off!', '2003-05-22 16:20:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(305100, 21753, 8530, '<td valign="top">Yup, flowers have definitely been a trend I didn''t notice -- I didn''t really skim the thumbs. Not your fault you''re the third one I''ve come across. It meets the topic, and actually the closeup focus and the predonderance of one of the colours over the other is a very nice touch that does not duplicate the earlier efforts. And yes, it does rather look like an apropos title. I also note the hovering-butterfly effect above the yellow bits, which definitely makes the picture more interesting to me. If it was intentional, good job. (If not, good job anyhow!)</td>', 'Yup, flowers have definitely been a trend I didn''t notice -- I didn''t really skim the thumbs. Not your fault you''re the third one I''ve come across. It meets the topic, and actually the closeup focus and the predonderance of one of the colours over the other is a very nice touch that does not duplicate the earlier efforts. And yes, it does rather look like an apropos title. I also note the hovering-butterfly effect above the yellow bits, which definitely makes the picture more interesting to me. If it was intentional, good job. (If not, good job anyhow!)', '2003-05-22 16:22:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(305101, 21826, 8530, '<td valign="top">Mmm. Salad.<br/> <br/>Darn you! Now I want salad. Good photograph, good use of color and placement and background. Did you consider slicing them? Probably best you didn''t, I would have been even mroe hungry.</td>', 'Mmm. Salad. Darn you! Now I want salad. Good photograph, good use of color and placement and background. Did you consider slicing them? Probably best you didn''t, I would have been even mroe hungry.', '2003-05-22 16:23:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(305107, 21963, 8530, '<td valign="top">Inasmuch as this is presumably a staged photo, I must compliment you on one of the more natural-seeming snapshots, that is, it feels like you just happened to find something that fit the topic criteria without needing to elaborately stage a setting. I do like photography-as-art, but I also like clever use of casual snapshots.</td>', 'Inasmuch as this is presumably a staged photo, I must compliment you on one of the more natural-seeming snapshots, that is, it feels like you just happened to find something that fit the topic criteria without needing to elaborately stage a setting. I do like photography-as-art, but I also like clever use of casual snapshots.', '2003-05-22 16:32:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(305108, 21676, 8530, '<td valign="top">Very prettily staged, particularly the crisp focus on the leaf with the blurred background. Good colour contrast.</td>', 'Very prettily staged, particularly the crisp focus on the leaf with the blurred background. Good colour contrast.', '2003-05-22 16:32:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(305109, 21824, 8530, '<td valign="top">Shots like this always amaze me, which, er, is partly because I''m very ignorant (not stupid, just ignorant). But still, nice, though I think I would have gone with a more yellow second colour to really get the contrast of the complementary colours -- this has a bit too much red in.</td>', 'Shots like this always amaze me, which, er, is partly because I''m very ignorant (not stupid, just ignorant). But still, nice, though I think I would have gone with a more yellow second colour to really get the contrast of the complementary colours -- this has a bit too much red in.', '2003-05-22 16:34:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(305110, 21938, 8530, '<td valign="top">I think perhaps the flower is a bit too pink-and-orange to truly emphasize the contrast of complementary colours, but good thinking (as you probably have seen by now this turns out to be a common theme) and good placement -- I like how the flower seems to jump out at you.</td>', 'I think perhaps the flower is a bit too pink-and-orange to truly emphasize the contrast of complementary colours, but good thinking (as you probably have seen by now this turns out to be a common theme) and good placement -- I like how the flower seems to jump out at you.', '2003-05-22 16:35:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(305125, 21412, 8530, '<td valign="top">Really a pity how many people chose a flower to demonstrate this, as it slightly takes away from this. I like this nice, water-flecked shot. The color contrast of the complementary colours is strong, and it''s a gorgeous-looking flower. The flaw is that the blurred background keeps drawing my eye despite the good center placement of the rest -- maybe a slightly closer crop would have been better.</td>', 'Really a pity how many people chose a flower to demonstrate this, as it slightly takes away from this. I like this nice, water-flecked shot. The color contrast of the complementary colours is strong, and it''s a gorgeous-looking flower. The flaw is that the blurred background keeps drawing my eye despite the good center placement of the rest -- maybe a slightly closer crop would have been better.', '2003-05-22 17:21:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(305126, 21708, 8530, '<td valign="top">Hmm. On the one hand, yes, you do have some complementary colours there. On the other hand, the softness of some of the colours and the fact that non-complementary colours are set next to each other between the pairings detracts from the focus on the topic. Also, honestly, photographs of money don''t do much for me. But it was an interesting idea.</td>', 'Hmm. On the one hand, yes, you do have some complementary colours there. On the other hand, the softness of some of the colours and the fact that non-complementary colours are set next to each other between the pairings detracts from the focus on the topic. Also, honestly, photographs of money don''t do much for me. But it was an interesting idea.', '2003-05-22 17:22:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(305129, 21963, 6660, '<td valign="top">Interesting foto and love the boys expression, and while this foto does meet the challenge, I do not feel it is a great example, as the green nor the red has helped to make the other colour stand out.</td>', 'Interesting foto and love the boys expression, and while this foto does meet the challenge, I do not feel it is a great example, as the green nor the red has helped to make the other colour stand out.', '2003-05-22 17:32:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(305130, 21983, 811, '<td valign="top">The curves are very graceful and I really like the bright, brilliant colors.</td>', 'The curves are very graceful and I really like the bright, brilliant colors.', '2003-05-22 17:32:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(305132, 21938, 811, '<td valign="top">I believe this is one of those "rare instances" where not following the rule of thirds adn centering your subject works well.</td>', 'I believe this is one of those "rare instances" where not following the rule of thirds adn centering your subject works well.', '2003-05-22 17:34:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(305133, 21774, 6660, '<td valign="top">I don''t think that this foto has met the challenge. I do not see any complementary colours here, let alone the one colour enhancing the other. Please excuse me If I have made a mistake and there is are complementary colours here</td>', 'I don''t think that this foto has met the challenge. I do not see any complementary colours here, let alone the one colour enhancing the other. Please excuse me If I have made a mistake and there is are complementary colours here', '2003-05-22 17:35:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(305134, 21929, 811, '<td valign="top">Very nice warm colors.  I also like the soft, subtle lighting.</td>', 'Very nice warm colors.  I also like the soft, subtle lighting.', '2003-05-22 17:36:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(305137, 21978, 811, '<td valign="top">I hoped that washed off okay. :-)  I think a lighter background, though the black adds an element of mystery, would have shown the blue hand better.</td>', 'I hoped that washed off okay. :-)  I think a lighter background, though the black adds an element of mystery, would have shown the blue hand better.', '2003-05-22 17:44:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(305138, 21740, 811, '<td valign="top">Good focus and lighting.  I think it would have benefited from a more dramatic angle or perspective.</td>', 'Good focus and lighting.  I think it would have benefited from a more dramatic angle or perspective.', '2003-05-22 17:45:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(305140, 21914, 811, '<td valign="top">Nice colors.  The focus seems a little grainy.  What was your ISO?</td>', 'Nice colors.  The focus seems a little grainy.  What was your ISO?', '2003-05-22 17:46:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(305141, 21847, 4122, '<td valign="top">GO SPURS!!!</td>', 'GO SPURS!!!', '2003-05-22 17:46:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(305145, 21657, 811, '<td valign="top">I like your use of depth of field.  Would it have been possible to get even cloer to one of the drops to catch a reflection in it?</td>', 'I like your use of depth of field.  Would it have been possible to get even cloer to one of the drops to catch a reflection in it?', '2003-05-22 17:50:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(305146, 21968, 811, '<td valign="top">very interesting composition.  Has a very "modern" abstract feeling to it.</td>', 'very interesting composition.  Has a very "modern" abstract feeling to it.', '2003-05-22 17:54:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(305149, 21992, 811, '<td valign="top">Reminds me of a science fair set up.  You have met the challenge, but the composition seems a little haphazard, and it is difficult to find any one thing you want me to focus on (maybe that was your point).  I think cropping the "table" at the bottom, and the stuff at the top would have helped some.</td>', 'Reminds me of a science fair set up.  You have met the challenge, but the composition seems a little haphazard, and it is difficult to find any one thing you want me to focus on (maybe that was your point).  I think cropping the "table" at the bottom, and the stuff at the top would have helped some.', '2003-05-22 17:57:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(305151, 21927, 811, '<td valign="top">I normally don''t like abstract shots, but this one is interesting.  I think it is the deep colors that I like.</td>', 'I normally don''t like abstract shots, but this one is interesting.  I think it is the deep colors that I like.', '2003-05-22 17:59:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(305156, 21988, 811, '<td valign="top">This would be a great bowling stock photo, or an add for Brunswick.  I appreciate the fact that you too the time to line up the words.  Your composition really draws the viewer into the picture.  Could the focus have been a touch sharper on the ones in the front?</td>', 'This would be a great bowling stock photo, or an add for Brunswick.  I appreciate the fact that you too the time to line up the words.  Your composition really draws the viewer into the picture.  Could the focus have been a touch sharper on the ones in the front?', '2003-05-22 18:07:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(305157, 21954, 811, '<td valign="top">Reminded me of red and green earthworms.  Good composition.  Lining up the bendable area gives a line for the eyes to follow.</td>', 'Reminded me of red and green earthworms.  Good composition.  Lining up the bendable area gives a line for the eyes to follow.', '2003-05-22 18:08:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(305159, 21500, 811, '<td valign="top">This is a nice picture with the fountain centered, but because of the building in the background, I think it would work a touch better to have the fountain more in the right of the frame with teh tall building balancing it on the left.  Right now, it feels a little unbalanced to me because there are lights and buildings, etc on the left, but just darkness adn what looks like trees on the right.</td>', 'This is a nice picture with the fountain centered, but because of the building in the background, I think it would work a touch better to have the fountain more in the right of the frame with teh tall building balancing it on the left.  Right now, it feels a little unbalanced to me because there are lights and buildings, etc on the left, but just darkness adn what looks like trees on the right.', '2003-05-22 18:10:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(305164, 21803, 811, '<td valign="top">I really like how the sun and tree balance eachother.</td>', 'I really like how the sun and tree balance eachother.', '2003-05-22 18:21:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(305165, 21578, 7778, '<td valign="top">The illusory effect of the concave/convex planes is interesting enough. I wonder, if this was intended or ''trouvee''? <br/> <br/>-What I''ve learned from this capture is how simple/conservative composition can promote study (by slowing the viewing).</td>', 'The illusory effect of the concave/convex planes is interesting enough. I wonder, if this was intended or ''trouvee''?  -What I''ve learned from this capture is how simple/conservative composition can promote study (by slowing the viewing).', '2003-05-22 18:24:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(305166, 21948, 811, '<td valign="top">Great composition.  I like the strength of the lines.</td>', 'Great composition.  I like the strength of the lines.', '2003-05-22 18:29:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(305167, 21503, 811, '<td valign="top">Great texture.  The horizontalness of it makes it feel a bit static to me.  Could you have tilted it a little to make it slightly more dramatic?</td>', 'Great texture.  The horizontalness of it makes it feel a bit static to me.  Could you have tilted it a little to make it slightly more dramatic?', '2003-05-22 18:31:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(305168, 21952, 811, '<td valign="top">This picture made my son (16 months) go, "Oh, mmmmmm."  Good response.  Wish the focus had been a little sharper on the blue one.</td>', 'This picture made my son (16 months) go, "Oh, mmmmmm."  Good response.  Wish the focus had been a little sharper on the blue one.', '2003-05-22 18:32:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(305169, 21714, 811, '<td valign="top">Took me a second there!  I was like how did he get all of them to "stick" together.  hahaha.  Great work on getting all of it equally focused.</td>', 'Took me a second there!  I was like how did he get all of them to "stick" together.  hahaha.  Great work on getting all of it equally focused.', '2003-05-22 18:34:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(305170, 21781, 811, '<td valign="top">I think the tire detracts from the overall composition, but I like the green grass.  Good colors.</td>', 'I think the tire detracts from the overall composition, but I like the green grass.  Good colors.', '2003-05-22 18:35:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(305171, 21960, 7778, '<td valign="top">Thought upon looking at this capture repeatedly (and not too fleetingly): the capture (by my evaluation) would lend itself perfectly to a serial shoot. Consider the blue and hemlock without the ''gorge'' on the right, then its mirrored variables, followed by the above...<br/> <br/>Thanks for such a visual treat.</td>', 'Thought upon looking at this capture repeatedly (and not too fleetingly): the capture (by my evaluation) would lend itself perfectly to a serial shoot. Consider the blue and hemlock without the ''gorge'' on the right, then its mirrored variables, followed by the above... Thanks for such a visual treat.', '2003-05-22 18:39:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(305238, 21948, 8530, '<td valign="top">Neat. Color/complementary colour/neutral, repeat. Very topical. Kinda strange to look at, though -- I''m wondering where it''s from.</td>', 'Neat. Color/complementary colour/neutral, repeat. Very topical. Kinda strange to look at, though -- I''m wondering where it''s from.', '2003-05-22 20:26:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(305239, 21965, 8530, '<td valign="top">I''m afraid this one didn''t grab me topically as much as some of the other flower pictures -- the colours are in fact complementary but the lack of vividness in them doesn''t make it quite as obvious. Also, for some reason, the flower itself looks actually rather scary.</td>', 'I''m afraid this one didn''t grab me topically as much as some of the other flower pictures -- the colours are in fact complementary but the lack of vividness in them doesn''t make it quite as obvious. Also, for some reason, the flower itself looks actually rather scary.', '2003-05-22 20:31:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(305242, 21657, 8530, '<td valign="top">Probably more to lighting than anything, the green colour in the background is more yellow than makes the best complementary colour setup for this. A more vivid background would have suited that better. Also, the blur in this case is rather distracting, even though I understand the desire to focus finely on the droplets.</td>', 'Probably more to lighting than anything, the green colour in the background is more yellow than makes the best complementary colour setup for this. A more vivid background would have suited that better. Also, the blur in this case is rather distracting, even though I understand the desire to focus finely on the droplets.', '2003-05-22 20:33:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(305245, 21947, 8530, '<td valign="top">This is a lovely picture, and the coluor combination is certainly attractive, but the shade of the purple is not quite as obviously ''complementary'' as a redder tone would have been.</td>', 'This is a lovely picture, and the coluor combination is certainly attractive, but the shade of the purple is not quite as obviously ''complementary'' as a redder tone would have been.', '2003-05-22 20:35:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(305247, 21842, 8530, '<td valign="top">This is very lovely but I''m afraid that despite the purple tone it doesn''t register as sharply complementary to me.</td>', 'This is very lovely but I''m afraid that despite the purple tone it doesn''t register as sharply complementary to me.', '2003-05-22 20:36:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(305248, 21960, 8530, '<td valign="top">This is interesting looking, but it is both rather too homogenous of spectra nd not intensely complementary enough to fit the topic well.</td>', 'This is interesting looking, but it is both rather too homogenous of spectra nd not intensely complementary enough to fit the topic well.', '2003-05-22 20:37:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(305250, 21993, 8530, '<td valign="top">Blue Curacao, by any chance?<br/> <br/>Very nice, and something I haven''t seen yet this round. I like choice of light direction as well; it nicely higlights the colours without introducing any real distraction.</td>', 'Blue Curacao, by any chance? Very nice, and something I haven''t seen yet this round. I like choice of light direction as well; it nicely higlights the colours without introducing any real distraction.', '2003-05-22 20:39:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(305251, 21781, 8530, '<td valign="top">Excellent! Red, green, and the nice neutrality of black, no distractions, and a natural-looking snapshot.</td>', 'Excellent! Red, green, and the nice neutrality of black, no distractions, and a natural-looking snapshot.', '2003-05-22 20:40:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(305253, 21962, 8530, '<td valign="top">Huh. Most of the non-intense coloured photographs so far have left me feeling like they missed the topic, but this one works somewhat better for some reason. The pink stands out very well against the pale yellow-to-green, which suggests you''ve hit the proper colour contrast. Very well done.</td>', 'Huh. Most of the non-intense coloured photographs so far have left me feeling like they missed the topic, but this one works somewhat better for some reason. The pink stands out very well against the pale yellow-to-green, which suggests you''ve hit the proper colour contrast. Very well done.', '2003-05-22 20:43:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(305254, 21742, 8530, '<td valign="top">My, yes, that certainly does qualify as complementary in terms of colour, but that is not a building I would want to look at regularly. It is, however, a good photo of it. The framing, I think, is somewhat distracting from the topical colours, as it''s very bright, but artistically it''s a nice touch.</td>', 'My, yes, that certainly does qualify as complementary in terms of colour, but that is not a building I would want to look at regularly. It is, however, a good photo of it. The framing, I think, is somewhat distracting from the topical colours, as it''s very bright, but artistically it''s a nice touch.', '2003-05-22 20:45:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(305256, 21966, 8530, '<td valign="top">Mmm, delicious looking! A fairly nice shot that could make a good postcard -- that''s not an insult, I promise!</td>', 'Mmm, delicious looking! A fairly nice shot that could make a good postcard -- that''s not an insult, I promise!', '2003-05-22 20:46:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(305258, 21986, 8530, '<td valign="top">Far too much green to capture the point elegantly. Better might have been red blooms in that vase, though of course the leaves themselves count -- maybe a neutral vase? But a nice, arty shot, I suppose.</td>', 'Far too much green to capture the point elegantly. Better might have been red blooms in that vase, though of course the leaves themselves count -- maybe a neutral vase? But a nice, arty shot, I suppose.', '2003-05-22 20:47:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(305259, 21866, 8530, '<td valign="top">I have never understood until now why people paint their houses that shade of blue. It''s to give photographers a way to enter good pictures into these contests! That''s a terrific example of complementary colours, almost precisely as contrasty as they get (I know purple is traditionally considered the complement of yellow, but that blue is actually closer to what I tend to picture it as).</td>', 'I have never understood until now why people paint their houses that shade of blue. It''s to give photographers a way to enter good pictures into these contests! That''s a terrific example of complementary colours, almost precisely as contrasty as they get (I know purple is traditionally considered the complement of yellow, but that blue is actually closer to what I tend to picture it as).', '2003-05-22 20:48:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(305261, 21714, 8530, '<td valign="top">Heh, cute. Very good choice of colour, though the cloudy background is kinda strange looking.</td>', 'Heh, cute. Very good choice of colour, though the cloudy background is kinda strange looking.', '2003-05-22 20:49:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(305262, 21989, 8530, '<td valign="top">Wow this is a very cool picture -- I always have the worst luck trying to capture lightning and so I always appreciate good shots of it -- I think in terms of hitting the depiction of the complementary colours it falls a bit short. Too much of the photo is taken up by the clouds and sky, which add nothing to the point.</td>', 'Wow this is a very cool picture -- I always have the worst luck trying to capture lightning and so I always appreciate good shots of it -- I think in terms of hitting the depiction of the complementary colours it falls a bit short. Too much of the photo is taken up by the clouds and sky, which add nothing to the point.', '2003-05-22 20:51:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(305263, 21477, 8530, '<td valign="top">The front focal blur rather eye-drawing, which works in the sense that it draws you more to the red/green contrast but does sort of take away from any focus on the bug.</td>', 'The front focal blur rather eye-drawing, which works in the sense that it draws you more to the red/green contrast but does sort of take away from any focus on the bug.', '2003-05-22 20:52:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(305264, 21920, 8530, '<td valign="top">This works. You have the orange/blue contrast and the black/white one, and the staging of the scene does not scream "Hi! I''m a big staged scene for the sake of a contest!" as I can imagine someone leaving a couple carelessly piled masks in that way.</td>', 'This works. You have the orange/blue contrast and the black/white one, and the staging of the scene does not scream "Hi! I''m a big staged scene for the sake of a contest!" as I can imagine someone leaving a couple carelessly piled masks in that way.', '2003-05-22 20:54:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(305265, 21500, 8530, '<td valign="top">It''s nice to see several pairings of complementary colours in this: the focal point, of course, with the light against the water, but also the orangey tone to the lights around the fountain, the yellow-and-blue sky, and the yellow-lit building against the sky. Plus it''s a nice twilight shot of a fountain.</td>', 'It''s nice to see several pairings of complementary colours in this: the focal point, of course, with the light against the water, but also the orangey tone to the lights around the fountain, the yellow-and-blue sky, and the yellow-lit building against the sky. Plus it''s a nice twilight shot of a fountain.', '2003-05-22 20:55:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(305266, 21929, 8530, '<td valign="top">Yummy tomatoes, but I think the contrast between the colour complements would have been highlighted better by tomatoes actually on a vine. The green seems a bit washed out and not as obvious as one might want for this topic.</td>', 'Yummy tomatoes, but I think the contrast between the colour complements would have been highlighted better by tomatoes actually on a vine. The green seems a bit washed out and not as obvious as one might want for this topic.', '2003-05-22 20:56:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(305268, 21992, 8530, '<td valign="top">Test if your commenters are colour blind! Ask them about the numbers.<br/> <br/>What a terrific way to do this. The contrast between the complementary colours is low but in this case that''s just exactly right.</td>', 'Test if your commenters are colour blind! Ask them about the numbers. What a terrific way to do this. The contrast between the complementary colours is low but in this case that''s just exactly right.', '2003-05-22 20:57:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(305269, 21894, 8530, '<td valign="top">Okay, you hit the topical requirement, but I''m afraid the actual composition hurts my eyes.</td>', 'Okay, you hit the topical requirement, but I''m afraid the actual composition hurts my eyes.', '2003-05-22 20:58:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(305270, 21949, 8530, '<td valign="top">Crunchy orange worms, my favorite snack!<br/> <br/>Nice. Very home-entertainment-magaziney, I could picture it as an ad (I like good commercial work, so this is a compliment). Or accompanying an article on, I don''t know, the evil of overly processed cheese. And very definitely topical.</td>', 'Crunchy orange worms, my favorite snack! Nice. Very home-entertainment-magaziney, I could picture it as an ad (I like good commercial work, so this is a compliment). Or accompanying an article on, I don''t know, the evil of overly processed cheese. And very definitely topical.', '2003-05-22 20:59:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(305271, 21503, 8530, '<td valign="top">But now you must answer this question: is that her natural hair colour? :)<br/> <br/>Good colour choice. A little strange in terms of layout -- it looks flat (I wouldn''t have known it was a hat without the title clue) and disconnected.</td>', 'But now you must answer this question: is that her natural hair colour? :) Good colour choice. A little strange in terms of layout -- it looks flat (I wouldn''t have known it was a hat without the title clue) and disconnected.', '2003-05-22 21:00:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(305272, 21798, 8530, '<td valign="top">Good colours, though I wonder if a darker green would have contrasted better. Does anyone actually wear that green hat? It looks like it would spoil nearly any skin tone. :) Angle of shot is good.</td>', 'Good colours, though I wonder if a darker green would have contrasted better. Does anyone actually wear that green hat? It looks like it would spoil nearly any skin tone. :) Angle of shot is good.', '2003-05-22 21:01:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(305274, 21661, 8530, '<td valign="top">Hmm, well, the boots are a bit on the brown side to make them the perfect complement of that blue, but okay. What IS that?</td>', 'Hmm, well, the boots are a bit on the brown side to make them the perfect complement of that blue, but okay. What IS that?', '2003-05-22 21:02:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(305276, 21596, 8530, '<td valign="top">Many, MANY flowers contrasting with leaves. Okay, that''s new this round. The angle of shot seems strange somehow but since I can''t quite put my finger on why I guess that''s not the world''s most helpful comment.</td>', 'Many, MANY flowers contrasting with leaves. Okay, that''s new this round. The angle of shot seems strange somehow but since I can''t quite put my finger on why I guess that''s not the world''s most helpful comment.', '2003-05-22 21:03:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(305277, 21774, 8530, '<td valign="top">Erm. Okay, the house is vaguely red-brick vs green-grass, I guess, but sicne the focal point appears to be far more on the fence I think this misses the opportunity of topical display. Plus a healthier lawn might have worked better for that.</td>', 'Erm. Okay, the house is vaguely red-brick vs green-grass, I guess, but sicne the focal point appears to be far more on the fence I think this misses the opportunity of topical display. Plus a healthier lawn might have worked better for that.', '2003-05-22 21:04:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(305279, 21952, 8530, '<td valign="top">I keep running into these perfect ad-like creations in this contest, it''s very neat. Nice, very mouth-watering, good colour choices.</td>', 'I keep running into these perfect ad-like creations in this contest, it''s very neat. Nice, very mouth-watering, good colour choices.', '2003-05-22 21:05:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(305282, 21954, 8530, '<td valign="top">Ow, my eyes.<br/> <br/>Okay, let''s try that again. Yes, yes that would fit the topic quite well. And they''re BENDY straws, which is not something I would have ever thought to photograph myself. Very bright, very intense. I think I kinda like it.</td>', 'Ow, my eyes. Okay, let''s try that again. Yes, yes that would fit the topic quite well. And they''re BENDY straws, which is not something I would have ever thought to photograph myself. Very bright, very intense. I think I kinda like it.', '2003-05-22 21:05:44.000000', NULL, 1);
