(305428, 21895, 8530, '<td valign="top">This is very surreal, but it''s a good implementation of the colour complements. I like the fade of light at the bottom, good angle of incoming light; it helps focus on the contrasting colours.</td>', 'This is very surreal, but it''s a good implementation of the colour complements. I like the fade of light at the bottom, good angle of incoming light; it helps focus on the contrasting colours.', '2003-05-23 01:51:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(305429, 21831, 8530, '<td valign="top">Both the colour and the positioning of the close element versus the nice landscape help the life ring to stand out. The brightness of the sky does slightly diminish the impact (there''s a lot of paler colour around the edges rather than a level of blue that matches the level of orange) but a different angle probably would not have worked as well for framing purposes so that''s probably fine.</td>', 'Both the colour and the positioning of the close element versus the nice landscape help the life ring to stand out. The brightness of the sky does slightly diminish the impact (there''s a lot of paler colour around the edges rather than a level of blue that matches the level of orange) but a different angle probably would not have worked as well for framing purposes so that''s probably fine.', '2003-05-23 01:54:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(305431, 21907, 8530, '<td valign="top">Kind of an odd angle -- I presume that''s a shoe atop the ball but it looks rather flatter than I''d expect. Colour choices are good, with matching intensities where the complementary colours meet.</td>', 'Kind of an odd angle -- I presume that''s a shoe atop the ball but it looks rather flatter than I''d expect. Colour choices are good, with matching intensities where the complementary colours meet.', '2003-05-23 01:55:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(305432, 21899, 8530, '<td valign="top">Oh, keen setup. I do wish the flames had been closer in size; the yellow part of the image somewhat outdistances the blue as is. But definitely a nice exercise in the contrast.</td>', 'Oh, keen setup. I do wish the flames had been closer in size; the yellow part of the image somewhat outdistances the blue as is. But definitely a nice exercise in the contrast.', '2003-05-23 01:56:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(305433, 21974, 8530, '<td valign="top">I''m really running out of things to say about flowers against grass. As with a couple others, I think this would have worked better with a redder tone to the flower, nad I think maybe less blur of the greenery, but it''s certainly topical and not by any means a bad shot.</td>', 'I''m really running out of things to say about flowers against grass. As with a couple others, I think this would have worked better with a redder tone to the flower, nad I think maybe less blur of the greenery, but it''s certainly topical and not by any means a bad shot.', '2003-05-23 01:57:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(305437, 21955, 8530, '<td valign="top">You are a very strange person. Well, as obviously very set up shots go, this one definitely wins in terms of ''most unusual'' -- it''s not terribly arty or commercial, it''s apparently just set up for the joke. Contrast wise between the sets of complementary colours, you did a fine job, particularly with the light angle given the orange the yellowish-fading-to-orange cast. About the only flaw perhaps is the white space is a little overwhelming -- maybe a slightly larger syringe with more blue would have cured this.</td>', 'You are a very strange person. Well, as obviously very set up shots go, this one definitely wins in terms of ''most unusual'' -- it''s not terribly arty or commercial, it''s apparently just set up for the joke. Contrast wise between the sets of complementary colours, you did a fine job, particularly with the light angle given the orange the yellowish-fading-to-orange cast. About the only flaw perhaps is the white space is a little overwhelming -- maybe a slightly larger syringe with more blue would have cured this.', '2003-05-23 01:59:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(305438, 21803, 8530, '<td valign="top">Fairly nice sunset shot, and nice fade of blue contrasting to yellow contrasting to the purple cast of the hills. The glare off the sun is a little jarring given the coolness of the other shades but for the sake of the colours of the sky I imagine unavoidable.</td>', 'Fairly nice sunset shot, and nice fade of blue contrasting to yellow contrasting to the purple cast of the hills. The glare off the sun is a little jarring given the coolness of the other shades but for the sake of the colours of the sky I imagine unavoidable.', '2003-05-23 02:00:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(305439, 21885, 8530, '<td valign="top">Wow, I''m curious to see how you set this up. Very funny. PIty the greens weren''t as bright as the red as the contrast of the complementary colours would have had a bit more impact, but this is a terrific way to hit the topic and provide a fun picture.</td>', 'Wow, I''m curious to see how you set this up. Very funny. PIty the greens weren''t as bright as the red as the contrast of the complementary colours would have had a bit more impact, but this is a terrific way to hit the topic and provide a fun picture.', '2003-05-23 02:01:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(305441, 21957, 8530, '<td valign="top">That is, indeed, a fork. I presume it''s there to keep the purple vs yellow complement from being entirely boring, and surprisingly you''ve managed to keep from detracting from topic by use of shades of lighting. The intensity of the colours is so strong and the neutrality of the fork shading as well that it works even though the fork is really the focal point. Very effective.</td>', 'That is, indeed, a fork. I presume it''s there to keep the purple vs yellow complement from being entirely boring, and surprisingly you''ve managed to keep from detracting from topic by use of shades of lighting. The intensity of the colours is so strong and the neutrality of the fork shading as well that it works even though the fork is really the focal point. Very effective.', '2003-05-23 02:03:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(305442, 21669, 8530, '<td valign="top">Ahh, excellent. A presumably-staged shot that has the air of spontaneity. Good colour choices, and nice interweaving between them.</td>', 'Ahh, excellent. A presumably-staged shot that has the air of spontaneity. Good colour choices, and nice interweaving between them.', '2003-05-23 02:04:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(305443, 21995, 8530, '<td valign="top">Oh, wow. I LOVE wax seals. That''s gorgeous, and it does hit the topic well.</td>', 'Oh, wow. I LOVE wax seals. That''s gorgeous, and it does hit the topic well.', '2003-05-23 02:04:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(305444, 21857, 6359, '<td valign="top">Here is my two cents.<br/>It meets the challenge.<br/>With title and just looking at the picture I focus <br/>on the young boy bouncing. <br/>I think if the focus was more on the colors it may have score<br/>higher with me.<br/>=5</td>', 'Here is my two cents.It meets the challenge.With title and just looking at the picture I focus on the young boy bouncing. I think if the focus was more on the colors it may have scorehigher with me.=5', '2003-05-23 02:04:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(305445, 21969, 8530, '<td valign="top">A very strange picture, and I''m afraid the colours are busy enough to not call to mind the topic. Seems an interesting Victorian/Asian sort of mix of costume but the busy-ness of it all detracts.</td>', 'A very strange picture, and I''m afraid the colours are busy enough to not call to mind the topic. Seems an interesting Victorian/Asian sort of mix of costume but the busy-ness of it all detracts.', '2003-05-23 02:05:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(305446, 21843, 6359, '<td valign="top">Here is my two cents.<br/>It meets the challenge.<br/>The focus point seems to be on the grade. <br/>Both colors look out of focus and it disturbs me.<br/>I like the positioning of the grade in respect to frame.<br/>The white border seem to take away from photo for me.<br/>=5</td>', 'Here is my two cents.It meets the challenge.The focus point seems to be on the grade. Both colors look out of focus and it disturbs me.I like the positioning of the grade in respect to frame.The white border seem to take away from photo for me.=5', '2003-05-23 02:05:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(305447, 21988, 8530, '<td valign="top">Ha! Good, very good. Alternating the colours works well, it''s an unexpected setting, and the surrounding scene and background support it without drawing the eye away from things.</td>', 'Ha! Good, very good. Alternating the colours works well, it''s an unexpected setting, and the surrounding scene and background support it without drawing the eye away from things.', '2003-05-23 02:06:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(305448, 21577, 8530, '<td valign="top">Nice match of colour intensity on the contrasting two complementary tones. If this was mere happenstance as seems likely, very good choice of angles so that each colour gets about half the space. (It''s good even if you did set it up, but it''s harder when you work with what''s there already, neh?)</td>', 'Nice match of colour intensity on the contrasting two complementary tones. If this was mere happenstance as seems likely, very good choice of angles so that each colour gets about half the space. (It''s good even if you did set it up, but it''s harder when you work with what''s there already, neh?)', '2003-05-23 02:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(305449, 21991, 8530, '<td valign="top">Hits the topic, and unfortunately, my limit on flower comments. Reasonably good framing and focus choices.</td>', 'Hits the topic, and unfortunately, my limit on flower comments. Reasonably good framing and focus choices.', '2003-05-23 02:08:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(305450, 21700, 8530, '<td valign="top">I think, honestly, I would have preferred this without the floaters against the leaves. The colours of red leaf upon green upon the terra-cotta background would have quite sufficed and hit the topic spot-on. The floater additions distract and detract and make it look like you couldn''t resist an arty touch that was wholly unnecessary. Mind you, it''s a solid base idea and a good photo overall, despite my criticism.</td>', 'I think, honestly, I would have preferred this without the floaters against the leaves. The colours of red leaf upon green upon the terra-cotta background would have quite sufficed and hit the topic spot-on. The floater additions distract and detract and make it look like you couldn''t resist an arty touch that was wholly unnecessary. Mind you, it''s a solid base idea and a good photo overall, despite my criticism.', '2003-05-23 02:10:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(305451, 21852, 8530, '<td valign="top">Nice apples, very delicious looking, and a good setup, angle, and lighting. But I''m afraid the use of the very red cloth rather than a more neutral tone (or something containing both colours) didn''t please me as much.</td>', 'Nice apples, very delicious looking, and a good setup, angle, and lighting. But I''m afraid the use of the very red cloth rather than a more neutral tone (or something containing both colours) didn''t please me as much.', '2003-05-23 02:12:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(305452, 21937, 8530, '<td valign="top">Huh. That''s... different. Well, you certainly do use complementary colours, and I suppose that it''s a good picture in general, but I''m still not quite sure what I really think of it.</td>', 'Huh. That''s... different. Well, you certainly do use complementary colours, and I suppose that it''s a good picture in general, but I''m still not quite sure what I really think of it.', '2003-05-23 02:13:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(305482, 21850, 6019, '<td valign="top">I really like this, there is a really nice balance to it and the only colours seemingly purple and yellow. Well done! 8</td>', 'I really like this, there is a really nice balance to it and the only colours seemingly purple and yellow. Well done! 8', '2003-05-23 03:19:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(305483, 21899, 6019, '<td valign="top">Clever, a blue candle would have been good too!!</td>', 'Clever, a blue candle would have been good too!!', '2003-05-23 03:20:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(305488, 21993, 6359, '<td valign="top">First impression:<br/>Glass filled with blue liquid, I cant make out if it is an actual drink or not.<br/> <br/>The photo meets the challenge with the two colors, blue/orange. Colors are good.<br/> <br/>A different border may be needed or none at all.<br/>I think a typical border is larger on the outside and small on the inside. That would have work better for me.<br/> <br/>Lighting may need to be diffused. By doing this, you will get less glare on the glass and there will be less highlights on material under glass.<br/> <br/>I would have like to see the focus closer to the orange slice.<br/>=5</td>', 'First impression:Glass filled with blue liquid, I cant make out if it is an actual drink or not. The photo meets the challenge with the two colors, blue/orange. Colors are good. A different border may be needed or none at all.I think a typical border is larger on the outside and small on the inside. That would have work better for me. Lighting may need to be diffused. By doing this, you will get less glare on the glass and there will be less highlights on material under glass. I would have like to see the focus closer to the orange slice.=5', '2003-05-23 04:02:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(305491, 21741, 6359, '<td valign="top">First impression:<br/>Nice colors<br/> <br/>It definitely meets the challenge<br/>This was pretty clever of you to make 4 lighters out of 2.<br/>The use of the mirror was great.<br/> <br/>Lighting  may need to have been diffused just a little.<br/>To me, it is washing out the top edges of the top lighter.<br/>The angle may have been the other solution.<br/> <br/>Once again, excellent job and my pick this week. <br/>=9</td>', 'First impression:Nice colors It definitely meets the challengeThis was pretty clever of you to make 4 lighters out of 2.The use of the mirror was great. Lighting  may need to have been diffused just a little.To me, it is washing out the top edges of the top lighter.The angle may have been the other solution. Once again, excellent job and my pick this week. =9', '2003-05-23 04:16:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(305492, 21500, 8682, '<td valign="top">WOW... GREAT</td>', 'WOW... GREAT', '2003-05-23 04:32:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(305493, 21781, 8682, '<td valign="top">Good focues</td>', 'Good focues', '2003-05-23 04:35:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(305497, 21756, 4569, '<td valign="top">Hola cielo, espero que no te haya importado que entrase en tu pág vieja para votarte, qué raro que no lo hubiéses hecho tú!, es que me gustaba mucho tu fresita y te merecías el 10, bss</td>', 'Hola cielo, espero que no te haya importado que entrase en tu pág vieja para votarte, qué raro que no lo hubiéses hecho tú!, es que me gustaba mucho tu fresita y te merecías el 10, bss', '2003-05-23 04:53:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(305505, 21894, 7010, '<td valign="top">Beautiful abstract shot! The colours came out very well. Sorry, I can only say nice things about this one ;o)<br/></td>', 'Beautiful abstract shot! The colours came out very well. Sorry, I can only say nice things about this one ;o)', '2003-05-23 05:25:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(305508, 21986, 4517, '<td valign="top">Excellent colours</td>', 'Excellent colours', '2003-05-23 05:30:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(305509, 21742, 7010, '<td valign="top">I like the contrast between the grey foreground and the rich colored background. It looks like this two elements are fighting each other for the viewers attention. The reflection is so clear it almost seems unreal. A tiny bit more sharpness would serve this image well imho. You did a fine job on the composition. Regards, Marco.</td>', 'I like the contrast between the grey foreground and the rich colored background. It looks like this two elements are fighting each other for the viewers attention. The reflection is so clear it almost seems unreal. A tiny bit more sharpness would serve this image well imho. You did a fine job on the composition. Regards, Marco.', '2003-05-23 05:31:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(305510, 21826, 4517, '<td valign="top">Nice pic, would like to see top of the red pepper.</td>', 'Nice pic, would like to see top of the red pepper.', '2003-05-23 05:31:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(305511, 21955, 4517, '<td valign="top">very original.8</td>', 'very original.8', '2003-05-23 05:34:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(305512, 21714, 4517, '<td valign="top">There`s no way you threw them up i the air like that. Must be a photo under the jacks. 8</td>', 'There`s no way you threw them up i the air like that. Must be a photo under the jacks. 8', '2003-05-23 05:36:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(305514, 21700, 4517, '<td valign="top">Good subject but background doesn`t look pretty. Would look better on plain background or even grass.</td>', 'Good subject but background doesn`t look pretty. Would look better on plain background or even grass.', '2003-05-23 05:38:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(305537, 21852, 7010, '<td valign="top">You did a very good job on the composition of this image. The apples are placed very well, wich results in a nicely balanced image. It shows that you did a big effort to compose this shot with care. <br/>I got a few remarks, though (if you don''t mind): <br/>- There is too little distinction between the cloth and the red apple, wich makes the green apple the most prominent element in this picture, while being placed on the background. This gives a kind of strange feel.<br/>- The stem of the red apple has the same colorcast as the apple itself. This gives the impression as if the image was painted over afterwards. It makes the fruit look a bit unnatural to me. On the other hand, it has given it (in combination with the velvet) a kind of ''retro-technicolor'' look, which ís nice (although not really my cup of tea ;o)<br/>- The red elements (apple and velvet) are a bit too dark imho.<br/> <br/>Regards, Marco.<br/> <br/></td>', 'You did a very good job on the composition of this image. The apples are placed very well, wich results in a nicely balanced image. It shows that you did a big effort to compose this shot with care. I got a few remarks, though (if you don''t mind): - There is too little distinction between the cloth and the red apple, wich makes the green apple the most prominent element in this picture, while being placed on the background. This gives a kind of strange feel.- The stem of the red apple has the same colorcast as the apple itself. This gives the impression as if the image was painted over afterwards. It makes the fruit look a bit unnatural to me. On the other hand, it has given it (in combination with the velvet) a kind of ''retro-technicolor'' look, which ís nice (although not really my cup of tea ;o)- The red elements (apple and velvet) are a bit too dark imho. Regards, Marco. ', '2003-05-23 06:29:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(305547, 21963, 7010, '<td valign="top">This boy looks very proud of being the captain of this vessel ;o)<br/>I like the clarity of this shot. Litteraly, you met the challenge by adding the grass on the foreground. Unfortunally, this is imho the weak aspect of this image. (in terms of composition, I mean). Also: the main point of interest of this shot is the boy, and not the color combination. Further on, I wouldn''t have cropped the boat on the right side, and wouldn''t have put the boy in the middle of the composition. <br/> <br/>Hopefully being helpfull...<br/>Regards, Marco.</td>', 'This boy looks very proud of being the captain of this vessel ;o)I like the clarity of this shot. Litteraly, you met the challenge by adding the grass on the foreground. Unfortunally, this is imho the weak aspect of this image. (in terms of composition, I mean). Also: the main point of interest of this shot is the boy, and not the color combination. Further on, I wouldn''t have cropped the boat on the right side, and wouldn''t have put the boy in the middle of the composition.  Hopefully being helpfull...Regards, Marco.', '2003-05-23 06:42:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(305550, 21803, 7010, '<td valign="top">Okay, you definitely WOW-ed me here... Nice observation. You did well on the composition and exposure. Challenge met. I\''m not completely sure about the tree and the blue border, though...<br/>Regards, Marco.</td>', 'Okay, you definitely WOW-ed me here... Nice observation. You did well on the composition and exposure. Challenge met. I\''m not completely sure about the tree and the blue border, though...Regards, Marco.', '2003-05-23 06:50:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(305555, 21676, 7010, '<td valign="top">Ooooooooooooooooh !! This is a beautiful shot. Very subtile and with style. Challenge met (although it could have been a tad more ''red''). Nice composition and good job on exposure. Welldone! <br/>Regards, Marco</td>', 'Ooooooooooooooooh !! This is a beautiful shot. Very subtile and with style. Challenge met (although it could have been a tad more ''red''). Nice composition and good job on exposure. Welldone! Regards, Marco', '2003-05-23 06:56:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(305558, 21969, 1368, '<td valign="top">wtf</td>', 'wtf', '2003-05-23 07:13:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(305559, 21971, 7010, '<td valign="top">When I saw the title, I thought: ''Great! He or she switched the caps of the markers to make an allusion on the movie'' ... and then I looked at the picture and I was a bit disappointed that I didn''t find any reference of that idea. But.. it''s a photography contest, and not a ''creative titling'' contest, so I won''t hold it against you, when scoring.<br/>Technically speaking, I''ve got two remarks:<br/>- the pens are not placed completely symmetrical. (Otherwise, if  this was your intention, the difference between the two is not prominent enough.) It gives a kind of ''sloppy'' impression.<br/>- the background color doesn''t match with the colors of the pens.<br/> <br/>You''ve got good detail and sharpness, and the challenge is met very well (although not very creatively imho)<br/> <br/>I hope that I not offended you with these comments. I honestly think you could do better than this. Regards, Marco.</td>', 'When I saw the title, I thought: ''Great! He or she switched the caps of the markers to make an allusion on the movie'' ... and then I looked at the picture and I was a bit disappointed that I didn''t find any reference of that idea. But.. it''s a photography contest, and not a ''creative titling'' contest, so I won''t hold it against you, when scoring.Technically speaking, I''ve got two remarks:- the pens are not placed completely symmetrical. (Otherwise, if  this was your intention, the difference between the two is not prominent enough.) It gives a kind of ''sloppy'' impression.- the background color doesn''t match with the colors of the pens. You''ve got good detail and sharpness, and the challenge is met very well (although not very creatively imho) I hope that I not offended you with these comments. I honestly think you could do better than this. Regards, Marco.', '2003-05-23 07:17:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(305561, 21932, 7010, '<td valign="top">Nice! The colors are very clear and vibrant, great detail, and nice capture of the flame. Composition also deserves a praise... Welldone!<br/>Regards, Marco</td>', 'Nice! The colors are very clear and vibrant, great detail, and nice capture of the flame. Composition also deserves a praise... Welldone!Regards, Marco', '2003-05-23 07:21:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(305601, 21947, 8130, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!  It seems cropped a little tight, but the lighting and colors make up for it!</td>', 'Beautiful!  It seems cropped a little tight, but the lighting and colors make up for it!', '2003-05-23 09:38:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(305605, 21477, 8130, '<td valign="top">Love the subject. The soft focus in the foreground is somewhat distracting, tho.</td>', 'Love the subject. The soft focus in the foreground is somewhat distracting, tho.', '2003-05-23 09:43:09.000000', NULL, 1),
